  static String? details(String category) {
    final values = byCategory[category];
    if (values == null) return null;
    final stone = values[1];
    final purpose = values[2];
    final heading = values[3];
    final letter = values[4];
    const closing =
        "Bringing harm to none as it comes.\nThis I accept, so mote it be.";
    return "PURPOSE\n$purpose\n\n"
        "MATERIALS NEEDED\nMason jar, black Sharpie, paper.\nRecommended optional sacred stone or jewelry: $stone.\nNo table, candles, or altar required.\n\n"
        "1. PREPARATION AT HOME\nIn a peaceful, quiet environment, use your black Sharpie to handwrite the entire sacred letter below onto paper, including the closing declaration. Read it carefully and memorize it if you wish. Fold the paper and carry it in your Mason jar.\n\n"
        "2. $heading — WRITE THIS COMPLETE LETTER\n$letter\n\n$closing\n\n"
        "3. ENTER THE UNIVERSE\nTravel to a peaceful, safe, legally accessible outdoor place beneath the open night sky. Feel the Earth beneath your feet and the air around you. Honor the Creator of the Universe, Ra as the Sun, and Thoth in his association with lunar wisdom. During a new moon, the Moon may not be visible.\n\n"
        "4. MEDITATE AND CONNECT\nHold your stone or wear your spiritual jewelry if you brought it. Settle your thoughts, breathe comfortably, and concentrate on your written prayer. Continue until you feel personally centered and connected in your heart. Do not force the experience.\n\n"
        "5. RECITE THREE TIMES\nRemove your letter from the Mason jar. Recite the entire written letter aloud three times, including its sacred closing. First, establish your intention. Second, deepen your focus. Third, recite with conviction. Memorization is encouraged but not required.\n\n"
        "6. RELEASE THE WRITTEN LETTER\nWhere permitted and safe, burn the paper only in a suitable fireproof vessel, with extinguishing water available, never inside an ordinary glass Mason jar, which can shatter. Do not burn in windy conditions. If fire is unsafe or prohibited, tear the paper into four pieces as a symbolic release.\n\n"
        "7. FOUR WINDS RELEASE\nHonor the directions in this order: NORTH, WEST, SOUTH, EAST. Face each direction and symbolically release your intention. Scatter only fully cold, extinguished ashes where legally permitted and environmentally appropriate; otherwise keep them contained and dispose of them responsibly.\n\n"
        "8. UNIVERSAL SACRED CLOSING\nPlace your hands over your heart and say once more:\n$closing\n\n"
